{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-61793",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The formula for exponential decay (in terms of a decay rate $r$) is\n\n$$\ny(t)=a(1-r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- $a=5\\,000$ is the initial population.\n\n- $r=0.03$ is the decay rate ($3%$ expressed as a decimal).\n\n- $t=$ the time, in years.\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $y$ is\n\n$$\ny(t)=5\\,000\\cdot (1-0.03)^{t}=5\\,000\\cdot (0.97)^{t}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
